MAIL -- where vi's mail helper looks====================================`read_mail' is elvis/vi's mail-reading helper.  It is invoked BY the editor,not from a command line, and it opens /dd/MAIL/mail_ and quotes what it findsso you can reply to it.`mail_' is here and EMPTY.  Without the file read_mail could not openanything and exited without a word, which is why it sat in the "silent for noknown reason" list for a long time.  With an empty mailbox it does exactlywhat it should: it reads to end-of-file and has nothing to quote.